# Wan-AI/Wan2.2-TI2V-5B-Diffusers: the UMT5 encoder is already BF16.
# The transformer and VAE source tensors are FP32. Keep Wan's time projections,
# normalization gains, modulation tables and velocity head in FP32.
# Patterns use the architecture's declared weight names.
#
# rad-convert <pinned Wan Diffusers directory> --recipe \
#     data/recipes/wan-2.2-ti2v-5b-bf16.recipe -o wan-2.2-ti2v-5b-bf16.rad
time.*                    cast dtype=f32
dit.head.*                cast dtype=f32
dit.block.*.table         cast dtype=f32
dit.block.*.cross_norm.*  cast dtype=f32
dit.block.*.norm_*.weight cast dtype=f32
dit.*                    cast dtype=bf16
text.*                   cast dtype=bf16
vae.*                    cast dtype=bf16
